"""
Streamlit dashboard for end-to-end lineage discovery -- calibrated
multi-signal tab classification.

Classifies each tab against reference tabs using up to three signals:
  1. column name similarity (fuzzy match)
  2. cell value overlap (Jaccard on unique values per column)
  3. cell formula signature (optional, slower -- function names + referenced
     sheet names used in formulas, compared the same way as values)

Instead of a hand-picked blend, weights are CALIBRATED from your reference
tabs: for each system with 2+ reference tabs, each signal is tested via
leave-one-out (does it correctly recognize a held-out reference as more
similar to its own system's other references than to any other system's?).
Signals that pass this test more often get more weight. The calibration
result (per-signal accuracy) is shown in the UI, not hidden -- that's what
keeps a blended score legible instead of a black box.

Run with:
    streamlit run lineage_dashboard.py
"""

